    "source": "Percé Rock (3)",
    "description": "Percé (2006 Population 3,419) is a small village near the tip of the Gaspé Peninsula in Québec. It has a long history of being an important seasonal fishing centre under the French. Today the area is mainly a tourist location particularly well-known for the attractions of Percé Rock and Bonaventure Island.\nPercé Rock is a natural rock formation located close to the shore facing the town. It is a natural tourist attraction for its size, color, and unusual door-like hole at one end the rock.",
